Description:

This is an attempt to replicate Zueuk's awesome "murl" Apophyisis plugin.
The result is not continuous, if the fractal is not symmetrical!
I do not know if it is really so useful, by the way it gives interesting effects
in my tests.
Use as a pretransform on symmetrical fractals. ONLY as pretransform, do not iterate it.
Be warned, murl projects the unit circle into the whole plane.
This optimized version has no parameters whatsoever, and supposes that order is two.
It is a lot faster than the general version

So use it properly!